at  person never had a gun  and they would say oh it was a phantom  gun it was something that really wasn't  there  so you have personally witnessed that  yes  a lot of these officers are latinos so  why are they targeting  other latinos is it racial profiling  self-loathing  they do racial profile it's like latino  gangs  they target other young latinos which is  what lisa vargas has contended all along  her 21 year old son anthony vargas who  aspired to be a chef  was shot 13 times by sheriff's deputies  while on his way home  you know we have videos with his voice  and his giggle and we have to play that  you know because we don't have his voice  no more we don't have  his smile lisa vargas filed a lawsuit  against the county of los  angeles and the deputies who shot her  son the suit  alleges that individuals who shot  anthony were members of the banditos  gang or prospects  and that membership in the banditos gang  included using excessive force  in shooting those who are unarmed they  have initiations  and in order for them to become a  prospect  their thing is they have to kill  somebody  anthony vargas was shot by sheriff  deputy nicolas perez and sheriff deputy  jonathan rojas are they also part of the  banditos gang or prospects for the  banditos  prospects yes they're prospects how do  you know  you know just personal conversations  with them and them saying that was one  of their main goals to be a part of this  gang  if you refuse to comply with their  demands to join the gang what happens  they stop giving you backup which is  very dangerous  they ignore you i have seen no evidence  of three or more deputies  engaging in a criminal activity with a  unifying symbol  whose primary purpose is to commit crime  l.a county sheriff alex villanueva has  publicly denied the existence of gangs  within his department on a video posted  to the lasd website  he warns the department's employees  against joining such groups  any employee who aligns with a click or  s